WEBVTT

00:03.470 --> 00:06.230
Why is Helvetica still alive?!

00:06.230 --> 00:09.860
This would be so easy if she were gone!

00:09.860 --> 00:12.730
What a pair of incompetent fools!

00:12.730 --> 00:14.680
I warned you.

00:14.680 --> 00:17.510
Our plan would've succeeded if not for them.

00:17.510 --> 00:19.000
You're the incompetent one.

00:19.000 --> 00:19.780
What?

00:19.780 --> 00:20.760
It's not over yet.

00:21.520 --> 00:24.750
We just have to kill this 
Helvetica girl, right?

00:25.710 --> 00:28.890
That's right. We haven't failed yet.

00:30.240 --> 00:31.340
Wait.

00:32.790 --> 00:36.300
I know a great way to upset Helvetica.

00:44.130 --> 00:45.860
Don't be absurd!

00:45.860 --> 00:48.010
I could never do something so cruel!

00:48.010 --> 00:50.140
Do it or we're done for.

00:50.140 --> 00:54.020
You should know all about 
the horrors of losing family.

00:55.900 --> 00:57.370
You can't be serious!

00:57.770 --> 01:00.830
Man, that S-rank party was something.

01:00.830 --> 01:03.340
Yeah. We barely suffered any damage.

01:03.340 --> 01:05.800
Was it a blessing from Vienna?

01:05.800 --> 01:06.590
Must've been.

01:07.590 --> 01:09.880
The cult of Vienna, Helvetica...

01:11.910 --> 01:17.870
They take happiness for granted, 
while I've lost everything.

01:19.490 --> 01:21.480
What we need is chaos.

01:21.480 --> 01:23.880
We're going to take down Helvetica.

01:37.490 --> 01:45.790
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

03:03.160 --> 03:08.580
<b>Episode 7 "A Long Night and a Bright Dawn"</b>

03:07.840 --> 03:08.980
Come in.

03:10.550 --> 03:13.100
Sorry to disturb you while you're resting.

03:13.100 --> 03:14.990
How is Ms. Angeline?

03:15.250 --> 03:18.140
Mr. Ashcroft, thank you for asking.

03:18.590 --> 03:21.210
She should be better after a night's sleep.

03:22.200 --> 03:23.360
Good.

03:23.920 --> 03:28.900
I don't know how to thank you
 for saving Bordeaux.

03:30.260 --> 03:32.650
You're giving us too much credit.

03:32.960 --> 03:37.110
Allow me to show my gratitude with this.

03:37.390 --> 03:38.770
What is that?

03:38.770 --> 03:40.760
An elven remedy.

03:40.760 --> 03:44.150
It's far more effective than any 
medicine produced by the empire.

03:44.150 --> 03:46.920
I can't accept something so valuable.

03:46.920 --> 03:49.710
It's hardly enough for all you've done,

03:49.710 --> 03:52.400
but it's the least I can do for you. Please.

03:53.170 --> 03:57.390
I see. In that case, I gratefully accept.

04:09.940 --> 04:12.960
Just smelling it makes me feel better.

04:20.850 --> 04:23.560
It'd be a waste 
not to make use of such a gift.

04:30.920 --> 04:32.710
What impressive effects.

04:34.380 --> 04:37.180
Well, I need to be
 in working shape tomorrow too.

04:42.000 --> 04:43.490
Talk about a pick-me-up.

04:52.340 --> 04:55.720
I'd like to you capture Count Malta alive.

04:55.970 --> 04:57.510
You can count on me.

04:57.510 --> 05:01.110
If he resists, I'll take an arm or three.

05:02.190 --> 05:04.640
I guess he doesn't have three arms to take.

05:09.050 --> 05:10.160
Hold!

05:12.670 --> 05:13.820
<i>This girl...</i>

05:14.160 --> 05:16.080
My name is Sasha Bordeaux.

05:16.560 --> 05:19.790
You're the one who defeated that shadow.

05:20.410 --> 05:22.340
Where are you headed at this hour?

05:23.860 --> 05:26.240
I heard the mansion was attacked.

05:26.240 --> 05:28.750
I thought I'd visit Lady Helvetica.

05:29.490 --> 05:34.770
I appreciate it, but we're not currently 
able to receive any guests.

05:34.770 --> 05:38.390
Don't mind me. 
I simply wish to pay my respects.

05:38.390 --> 05:41.910
I'd ask that you try again in the morning.

05:43.470 --> 05:44.660
Byaku!

05:44.660 --> 05:46.990
She's noticed. We should kill her.

05:48.380 --> 05:51.490
Blame yourself for not quite
 being sharp enough.

05:51.800 --> 05:52.870
Scum!

05:58.500 --> 05:59.630
Curse you!

06:03.190 --> 06:05.630
<i>He's firing magic, but I can't see a thing.</i>

06:06.930 --> 06:08.710
<i>If I'm not careful, I'll be done for.</i>

06:13.770 --> 06:15.930
You don't have time to be surprised.

06:26.650 --> 06:27.770
Goodbye.

06:35.590 --> 06:37.700
Ash! Mr. Elmore!

06:37.700 --> 06:39.120
How did you find me?

06:39.120 --> 06:44.010
The soldiers were concerned 
that only your horse returned.

06:44.010 --> 06:45.510
Bastards!

06:46.630 --> 06:48.430
You weren't invited.

06:51.590 --> 06:54.090
What did you do? I didn't see anything!

06:58.770 --> 07:00.990
Stay out of this, old man.

07:05.610 --> 07:07.660
I won't let a single one of you escape.

07:07.960 --> 07:09.650
You're all dead.

07:13.860 --> 07:16.260
Stay away...

07:19.880 --> 07:23.180
Run! You don't stand a chance against him!

07:33.680 --> 07:34.970
Ms. Ange!

07:41.120 --> 07:43.100
How dare you bully my friends.

07:43.540 --> 07:44.980
You, huh?

07:48.260 --> 07:49.870
I want to play, too.

07:49.870 --> 07:51.170
This is nonsense.

08:02.720 --> 08:06.060
I feel strangely good. I wonder why.

08:08.650 --> 08:13.270
<i>A similar shadow called to me in my dream.</i>

08:13.790 --> 08:18.490
<i>Next, a warm hand reached out to me.
 I thought it was my dad.</i>

08:18.490 --> 08:21.090
<i>I was enveloped in a
 mysterious woodland smell.</i>

08:21.770 --> 08:23.060
<i>And then...</i>

08:28.310 --> 08:31.070
I'm thinking. Stop interrupting me.

08:31.640 --> 08:33.210
Don't underestimate me.

08:36.090 --> 08:37.750
A three-dimensional magic square!

08:37.750 --> 08:39.950
Is that what he was hiding?

08:40.350 --> 08:44.850
Yes. Three-dimensional magic 
squares are high-level magic,

08:44.850 --> 08:48.070
but they require tremendous
mana and mental strength.

08:48.680 --> 08:51.910
Is that fancy trick the best you can do?

09:08.600 --> 09:12.080
Huh. They're faster and heavier 
now that they're visible,

09:12.080 --> 09:14.200
but I can easily predict your trajectories—

09:14.200 --> 09:16.600
So some of them move independently.

09:18.050 --> 09:21.880
If you need to use tricks,
you must be weaker than me.

09:22.400 --> 09:24.660
Huh? The pain's already gone.

09:25.400 --> 09:28.750
Of course! It must be 
the power of my dad's love!

09:48.630 --> 09:50.490
I have questions for you.

09:50.490 --> 09:52.890
Who are you, and what do you want?

09:53.130 --> 09:55.420
I could ask you the same thing.

09:55.420 --> 09:56.900
Who the hell are you?

09:57.260 --> 10:00.900
I am Ange, daughter of 
Belgrieve the Red Ogre.

10:01.770 --> 10:05.770
You're <i>whose</i> daughter? Don't screw with me!

10:12.730 --> 10:15.160
Why is it always you?

10:16.360 --> 10:17.810
What're you talking about?

10:18.170 --> 10:20.540
Are you not human?

10:28.010 --> 10:30.180
Seriously, what are you?

10:30.180 --> 10:31.820
Some new kind of monster?

10:35.910 --> 10:38.820
I'm like you.

10:42.300 --> 10:43.570
Shoot.

10:43.890 --> 10:45.230
He escaped.

10:50.360 --> 10:53.090
<i>Those strange clouds again.</i>

10:53.380 --> 10:55.840
<i>This fight isn't over yet.</i>

10:59.010 --> 11:01.430
Huh? Where's Ange?

11:01.430 --> 11:04.770
She suddenly woke and flew out of bed.

11:04.770 --> 11:06.730
Asked us to hold down the fort.

11:07.710 --> 11:08.600
You mean...

11:08.920 --> 11:11.590
I'm worried about Lady Helvetica. Let's go.

11:12.110 --> 11:13.620
It's an emergency, everyone!

11:14.240 --> 11:15.520
What's the matter?

11:15.790 --> 11:18.280
More dark clouds have gathered.

11:18.280 --> 11:20.460
If they come, it'll be tonight.

11:20.460 --> 11:22.340
Just as I thought.

11:22.340 --> 11:24.670
Helvetica, Sasha is...

11:24.880 --> 11:30.190
Sending her alone to capture him 
may have been a mistake.

11:33.320 --> 11:36.420
Milady! There are more undead.

11:37.240 --> 11:38.700
They're here?

11:38.700 --> 11:40.430
Remain calm and dispatch them.

11:40.430 --> 11:41.420
At once.

11:41.420 --> 11:43.210
We'll help, too.

11:43.210 --> 11:45.420
I'm still itching to fight!

11:47.910 --> 11:49.420
I'll go with them as well.

11:53.230 --> 11:54.680
What's wrong?

11:54.680 --> 11:58.430
I'd like you stay with me.

11:58.740 --> 12:01.790
I feel anxious without Sasha and Ash.

12:03.170 --> 12:06.900
Very well. I'm not that strong, 
but I shall protect you.

12:08.060 --> 12:11.040
They should be fine outside with those two.

12:11.320 --> 12:12.980
How very dependable.

12:13.720 --> 12:15.270
Let's move.

12:15.270 --> 12:18.300
If we need to flee, we'll be 
trapped on the second floor.

12:21.670 --> 12:23.430
Anyone here on the second floor—

12:33.630 --> 12:37.110
Most of the undead outside 
should be defeated.

12:37.110 --> 12:40.320
Take everyone left in the mansion
 and find Ane and Miri.

12:40.630 --> 12:43.560
I will. But what will you do, Mr. Belgrieve?

12:45.150 --> 12:48.570
I'll hold this off until you can get outside.

12:53.210 --> 12:54.030
Hurry!

12:54.030 --> 12:57.540
Ms. Angeline would be
 devastated if you fell in battle!

12:57.770 --> 13:02.710
I'm the one who taught her that, 
above all else, an adventurer must live.

13:02.710 --> 13:05.870
I'd never be able to face her if I died here.

13:08.230 --> 13:09.310
Good luck.

13:10.690 --> 13:12.680
Seren, let's go.

13:12.680 --> 13:13.500
Okay.

13:14.020 --> 13:14.810
Now then...

13:19.440 --> 13:22.050
<i>My body feels freakishly light.</i>

13:22.050 --> 13:24.160
<i>Is this the effect of the elven remedy?</i>

13:25.740 --> 13:26.580
Too slow!

13:35.000 --> 13:36.580
Is that all?

13:43.690 --> 13:45.830
We met at the tavern.

13:45.830 --> 13:48.140
Are you all right? This place is dangerous—

13:48.140 --> 13:49.480
Stay back!

13:49.800 --> 13:52.730
Everyone keeps interfering with my plans...

13:52.730 --> 13:54.730
Why do they have to do this?!

13:55.560 --> 13:56.970
Are you...

13:56.970 --> 13:58.350
Die!

14:04.120 --> 14:06.900
Everyone from this wing is here.

14:10.840 --> 14:12.390
It's all right.

14:12.390 --> 14:15.110
The adventurers are dispatching the threat.

14:15.110 --> 14:16.820
Now, let us go.

14:18.880 --> 14:21.490
<i>All I can do is offer mere consolations.</i>

14:22.390 --> 14:26.420
<i>I've made decent progress since I took 
over after my father's passing.</i>

14:26.420 --> 14:28.680
<i>I've gained people's trust.</i>

14:29.480 --> 14:31.670
<i>Perhaps it made me arrogant.</i>

14:32.340 --> 14:37.430
<i>I ignored the nobles opposing me,
believing the problem would resolve itself.</i>

14:37.750 --> 14:44.180
<i>The citizen's lives change according 
to those who stand above them.</i>

14:44.450 --> 14:47.770
<i>I can easily imagine how 
things would turn out</i>

14:47.770 --> 14:50.300
<i>with someone as power-hungry
 as Malta in control.</i>

14:50.690 --> 14:57.260
<i>But if I'm too preoccupied with my own 
scruples, then I can't govern properly.</i>

14:59.100 --> 15:03.550
<i>Surely my father bore this burden as well.</i>

15:11.690 --> 15:14.360
Good. You're all okay.

15:15.190 --> 15:16.470
Where's Mr. Bel?

15:16.830 --> 15:19.840
He's fighting so we could get away.

15:19.840 --> 15:22.550
What? We have to go help him!

15:22.550 --> 15:24.440
Mr. Bel will be fine.

15:24.440 --> 15:26.940
Besides, we have to defend this area.

15:27.600 --> 15:28.860
Right.

15:28.860 --> 15:31.290
Where in the world did Ange get off to?

15:35.080 --> 15:36.380
There's more of them.

15:37.340 --> 15:38.590
Sister!

15:38.590 --> 15:40.300
Th-That's...

15:44.400 --> 15:47.130
Father...

15:48.670 --> 15:51.380
No... it can't be.

15:51.650 --> 15:53.220
How heartless!

15:55.260 --> 15:58.130
Undead perish when their heads are destroyed.

15:58.870 --> 16:00.470
<i>This is a test.</i>

16:00.470 --> 16:04.730
<i>Even a lady must face realities
 she would rather not see.</i>

16:05.980 --> 16:07.520
Don't push yourself.

16:07.520 --> 16:10.540
No, this is my responsibility.

16:11.280 --> 16:18.100
<i>Father, now I shall take up 
the mantle you had to bear!</i>

16:24.540 --> 16:25.740
Stop this!

16:27.120 --> 16:29.780
<i>If I just keep defending, I'll never last.</i>

16:29.780 --> 16:31.630
<i>But I'm fighting a mere child.</i>

16:31.630 --> 16:33.420
How dare you dodge all my attacks.

16:41.960 --> 16:43.310
What is this?!

16:45.490 --> 16:46.850
What's happening?

16:47.230 --> 16:48.770
No, I don't want this!

16:48.770 --> 16:51.610
Help me, Father! Mother!

16:51.930 --> 16:54.490
<i>Cutting off her arm would save her, but...</i>

16:55.030 --> 16:57.770
<i>I know! Would this work?</i>

17:11.810 --> 17:12.910
Are you all right?

17:14.610 --> 17:15.670
That was scary...

17:16.270 --> 17:18.190
That was so scary!

17:21.740 --> 17:24.960
<i>Now she's acting like a kid her age.</i>

17:28.770 --> 17:29.700
Let's go.

17:36.000 --> 17:38.190
Th-Thank you.

17:44.210 --> 17:45.700
Dad!

17:48.480 --> 17:50.470
Ange! You're all right.

17:50.470 --> 17:53.890
Yeah. I'm glad you are too, Dad.

17:53.890 --> 17:55.700
I mean, I knew you would be.

17:58.100 --> 18:00.210
Those useless fools!

18:00.480 --> 18:03.900
If they haven't contacted me, 
does that mean they've failed?

18:03.900 --> 18:05.020
Count Malta.

18:05.770 --> 18:08.810
Where are you going alone at this hour?

18:10.000 --> 18:11.680
We're dealing with an emergency.

18:11.680 --> 18:13.570
I thought I'd help patrol.

18:13.940 --> 18:17.100
How admirable. You must be exhausted.

18:17.100 --> 18:19.020
There's wine at the guard station.

18:19.020 --> 18:20.560
Why don't you rest there?

18:20.560 --> 18:22.590
Ah, yes.

18:23.110 --> 18:25.700
<i>My soldiers will be at the station.</i>

18:25.700 --> 18:28.580
<i>I suppose I should meet up with them.</i>

18:28.930 --> 18:30.760
In that case, show me the way.

18:30.760 --> 18:31.330
Yes, milord.

18:35.190 --> 18:37.960
This is the officer's lounge.

18:37.960 --> 18:39.020
Very good.

18:41.480 --> 18:44.090
Thank you for coming.

18:45.160 --> 18:47.780
Lady Helvetica...

18:48.500 --> 18:50.100
Wh-What's the meaning of this?

18:50.100 --> 18:54.850
You should've lived quietly in Hazel.

18:54.850 --> 18:57.150
What? What are you talking about?

18:57.150 --> 18:59.010
What are you accusing me of?

18:59.010 --> 19:02.490
You know precisely what, don't you?

19:06.670 --> 19:11.490
W-Wait! If you kill me without proof, 
you'll lose the people's trust!

19:11.490 --> 19:14.260
They'll find out sooner or later.

19:14.260 --> 19:17.010
Th-This is tyranny!

19:17.010 --> 19:22.150
My naïveté invited this incident.

19:22.150 --> 19:26.140
But your foul plotting steeled my resolve.

19:26.390 --> 19:30.090
You think you'll get away with this?!

19:30.090 --> 19:32.460
I'm a nobleman of a dukedom!

19:32.460 --> 19:34.390
My blood is different from yours!

19:34.640 --> 19:37.640
Yes, and I'm glad of it.

19:37.640 --> 19:43.290
The very thought of sharing blood 
with you makes my skin crawl.

19:44.780 --> 19:47.620
Leave his body by the roadside.

19:48.270 --> 19:51.140
The valiant Count Malta was killed

19:51.140 --> 19:55.550
by scoundrels while he was
 out patrolling alone.

20:07.200 --> 20:09.570
What are you doing, Ange?

20:10.130 --> 20:13.070
Filling up on dad energy while I can.

20:13.810 --> 20:15.750
What good is that?

20:15.750 --> 20:17.160
It makes me strong!

20:17.160 --> 20:18.350
I see.

20:18.930 --> 20:21.060
Well, I should get going.

20:21.370 --> 20:24.250
Master, I'm disappointed 
we didn't get to duel.

20:24.250 --> 20:25.310
Until next time!

20:25.310 --> 20:27.990
Thank you so much for your help.

20:27.990 --> 20:30.200
I do hope you'll come again.

20:30.200 --> 20:34.350
Lady Sasha, please take care
 of yourself first.

20:34.350 --> 20:37.040
And thank you, Lady Seren.

20:37.040 --> 20:38.200
Dad.

20:38.500 --> 20:40.800
Won't you come with us to Orphen?

20:40.800 --> 20:43.230
We could find a big place to rent together.

20:44.900 --> 20:46.720
I'm really touched.

20:47.510 --> 20:48.480
Then...

20:48.480 --> 20:52.190
But if I moved, you'd never 
visit Turnera again.

20:52.920 --> 20:54.470
You mean...

20:54.790 --> 20:57.780
I consider Turnera our home.

20:57.780 --> 21:02.330
I'd like to keep protecting it
 so you can come back anytime.

21:02.330 --> 21:04.200
You love Turnera, don't you?

21:05.200 --> 21:06.700
Yeah, I do.

21:08.190 --> 21:09.760
I'll do my best.

21:09.760 --> 21:12.610
I'll work hard so I can come home next fall.

21:12.610 --> 21:14.150
Me, too!

21:14.150 --> 21:15.540
We'll come by with her.

21:15.540 --> 21:17.660
Mr. Belgrieve!

21:20.220 --> 21:21.710
I made it in time...

21:21.710 --> 21:23.410
Lady Helvetica.

21:23.410 --> 21:26.170
I do hope you'll visit us again.

21:26.450 --> 21:28.000
I'll be waiting for you.

21:28.000 --> 21:29.460
Thank you.

21:29.460 --> 21:30.540
You honor me with—

21:33.320 --> 21:37.470
I'll settle for your cheek for now, 
but next time...

21:37.890 --> 21:40.650
Please don't tease me too much.

21:40.650 --> 21:41.880
Dad...

21:42.230 --> 21:44.950
Are you looking for breasts after all?!

21:44.950 --> 21:47.000
What are you talking about?

21:51.100 --> 21:52.370
Well, I'm off.

21:53.060 --> 21:53.990
Okay.

21:55.280 --> 21:57.110
Take care now, Dad.

21:58.440 --> 22:00.390
Yeah. I'll see you again.

23:35.060 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.010
<b>"Meeting the Inhabitants of the Woods"</b>
